            <ArticleTitle>A method for the machine detection of near equivalence of major substructures in a molecule.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>129-139</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/jcc.540070205</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The use of the concept of near equivalence of substructures in a computer program concerned with organic synthesis requires a concrete definition of «nearness» and an efficient method for implementing the concept. Such a method has been devised and its use is described and examples are given.</AbstractText>
